from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;r=json.loads((P/'results.json').read_text());pct=lambda x:f'{x*100:.2f}%';pp=lambda x:f'{x*100:+.2f} pp';types=['WR-WR','WR-TE','RB-RB','RB-WR','QB-WR','QB-TE']
lines=['# How often do two teammates come close to their pregame P90?','','**In this small stored sample, two same-team receivers both reached 90% of their own pregame P90 in 13 of 756 WR-WR pairs (1.72%). Comparable different-game receivers were about as likely to do it. QB–receiver pairs behaved differently and reached together more often. There is no evidence here for a universal same-team penalty.**','','This is retrospective, exploratory evidence from **972 canonical offensive player-games, 47 distinct NFL games and five weeks (2026 weeks 1–5)**. Coverage is uneven: 280 player-games in week1, 146 in week2, only20 in week3, 267 in week4 and259 in week5. Pair rows share players/games; 756 pairs are not 756 independent trials. Five raw week clusters (four after matching) cannot establish a durable optimizer policy or precise significance. No live projections/settings/optimizer behavior changed.','','## Definitions frozen before outcomes','','“Close” means actual DK points ≥ **0.90 × stored P90**. Exact P90 exceedance and 0.80 sensitivity are also shown. P90 is a marginal forecast quantile, not a maximum, and 90% of P90 is not the 81st percentile. All included P90 values are ≥5 points; small/zero/negative forecasts are excluded with counts.','', 'Pre-kickoff storage is verified for projection row, projection run, model, feature row and feature run; cutoff and training cutoff must precede storage/kickoff as applicable. For a pair, both forecasts must exist before the earlier kickoff. Latest eligible stored projection per canonical player/game wins, with deterministic tie-breaking; optimizer repeats do not multiply observations. Aware timestamps are preserved. Naive legacy salary timestamps are conservatively interpreted in America/New_York; no four-hour correction creates extra eligible data. Schedule kickoff is reconstructed from already stored nflverse gameday/time in America/New_York, not fabricated from the week number.','','## First check: marginal calibration','','| Position | Player-games | ≥P90 | ≥90% P90 | ≥80% P90 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for pos,v in r['marginals'].items():lines.append(f"| {pos} | {v['1.0']['n']} | {pct(v['1.0']['rate'])} | {pct(v['0.9']['rate'])} | {pct(v['0.8']['rate'])} |")
lines+=['','Stored P90s were exceeded more than 10% in this sample, particularly QB. Therefore a blind independence assumption of 10% ×10%=1% is inappropriate. Ties count as hits. Calibration is conditional on this selected stored pool, not every NFL player or future model version.','','## Same team: absolute joint rates and empirical marginal comparison','','| Pair | Pairs | Distinct games / weeks | Both ≥P90 | Both ≥90% P90 | Both ≥80% P90 | Empirical marginal product at 90% | 90% joint week-bootstrap range |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for typ in types:
 v=r['pairs']['same_team|'+typ];a=v['0.9'];lo,hi=a['week_bootstrap_95'];lines.append(f"| {typ} | {a['pairs']} | {a['games']} / {a['weeks']} | {pct(v['1.0']['joint'])} | {pct(a['joint'])} | {pct(v['0.8']['joint'])} | {pct(a['empirical_independent_product'])} | {pct(lo)}–{pct(hi)} |")
lines+=['','The product uses the empirical hit rate of each side in that exact pair group. It is a descriptive reference; repeated appearances weight players and do not create independence. QB-WR/QB-TE show positive co-exceedance relative to these empirical marginals; RB-RB is rarer. WR-WR is slightly below its own marginal product, but that alone does not establish a worse roster choice.','','## Matched different-game comparisons','','Primary controls match season/week, ordered position pair, each player’s forecast mean in fixed five-point bins and salary in fixed $1,000 bins. Same-position sides are sorted by mean/salary/canonical ID. One deterministic different-game comparator is selected per matched same-team pair using identity hashes, never outcomes. Controls can be reused; unique control counts are retained. Both forecasts predate the earlier kickoff. Matching is partial and observational.','','| Pair | Matched / all same-team pairs | Same-team close rate | Different-game close rate | Difference | Paired week-cluster 95% range |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for typ in types:
 m=r['matched'][typ];a=m['same_team']['0.9'];b=m['different_game']['0.9'];d=m['paired_differences']['0.9'];lo,hi=d['week_cluster_bootstrap_95'];lines.append(f"| {typ} | {a['pairs']} / {r['matchcoverage'][typ]['same_team_pairs']} | {pct(a['joint'])} | {pct(b['joint'])} | {pp(d['difference'])} | {pp(lo)} to {pp(hi)} |")
lines+=['','Bootstrap resamples the four matched whole-week clusters 1,000 times with seed 20261016, preserving within-week player/game overlap and matching. These are coarse descriptive ranges with very few clusters, not evidence of causal or persistent statistical superiority. Controls may share a player with their treatment pair, reflecting one possible replacement; this is not a nine-player lineup solve.','','### Workload and availability sensitivity','','Model-linked original feature rows do retain some pregame context. A secondary sensitivity additionally matches exact recorded injury-status label (missing stays UNKNOWN) and opportunity proxy bins: two targets for WR/TE, five carries for RB, QB not applicable. These are stored lagged/model-input workload proxies, not future actual targets. This secondary specification was added after inspecting initial simple-match rates, without searching bin choices or thresholds for a desired result; treat it as exploratory.','','| Pair | Matched pairs | Same team | Different games | Difference |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for typ in types:
 m=r['richmatched'][typ];a=m['same_team']['0.9'];b=m['different_game']['0.9'];lines.append(f"| {typ} | {m['matched']} | {pct(a['joint'])} | {pct(b['joint'])} | {pp(a['joint']-b['joint'])} |")
lines+=['',f"Feature coverage out of 972: `{r['feature_coverage']}`. Availability probabilities are stored model inputs, not independently verified game-clearance probabilities. Missing status is not treated as healthy. Full practice/game clearance and per-source publication proof are incomplete. Current source tables cannot retroactively make these old snapshots more informed.",'','## Opposing same-game and different-game raw controls','','| Pair | Opposing pairs | Opposing close rate | Different-game pairs | Different-game close rate |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for typ in types:
 a=r['pairs']['opposing_same_game|'+typ]['0.9'];b=r['pairs']['different_game|'+typ]['0.9'];lines.append(f"| {typ} | {a['pairs']} | {pct(a['joint'])} | {b['pairs']} | {pct(b['joint'])} |")
lines+=['','These raw controls are not the matched results. Opponent-side and different-game counts also share observations and must not be read as independent sample sizes.','','## Salary and contribution, not nine simultaneous ceiling hits','','| Pair | Matched same-team mean salary | Different-game salary | Same-team actual combined points | Different-game actual points |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for typ in types:
 m=r['matched'][typ];a=m['same_team']['0.9'];b=m['different_game']['0.9'];lines.append(f"| {typ} | ${a['mean_salary']:,.0f} | ${b['mean_salary']:,.0f} | {a['mean_actual_points']:.2f} | {b['mean_actual_points']:.2f} |")
lines+=['','A lineup can succeed with two receivers contributing useful points without either reaching P90. Cheap same-team players may preserve salary for a stronger player elsewhere; these pair tables do not price that full-lineup tradeoff or contest payout. They also include backups/nonparticipants, rather than only optimizer-selected high-volume starters. No universal teammate cap, fixed penalty, tail-credit weight, or calibrated joint probability should be activated from this study. The useful next step is a frozen-pool, matched lineup comparison with observed inputs and prospective joint calibration.','','## Coverage, scoring and chronology limits','','29,237 original 2026 forecast rows collapse to2,873 unique eligible pregame player-games before offensive salary/P90/outcome filters. All 2024/25 forecasts inventoried were stored in2026 and excluded as postgame reconstructions. The empty2026 target.dim_game/target.fact_player_game_actual tables were not mistaken for absent source data: existing public raw schedule/stat records were linked through canonical nflreadpy native-ID aliases. No display-name joins. Five ambiguous/unmapped raw outcome identities were excluded.','',f"Exclusion counts (different stages/units): `{r['exclusions']}`. Participation among included player-games: `{r['participation']}`. Confirmed nonparticipants without stat rows contribute zero; missing outcomes are not silently zero. Including known DNP outcomes is intentional unconditional forecast evaluation, not a claim of pregame game-dressing clearance. A participants-only analysis would condition on postgame information and answer a different question.",'','Actual scoring version `research_dk_offense_unfloored_v1` is pinned in analyze.py: 0.04 passing yards/4 passing TD/−1 interception; 0.1 rushing and receiving yards, six TD, PPR, two-point conversions, six special-teams/fumble-recovery TD, −1 authoritative total fumbles lost, separate300/100/100-yard bonuses, no zero floor. Required components must be explicit; missing values exclude the record. This corrects the older shared-scorer default zero floor and checks the current raw schema’s special_teams_tds/fumbles_lost_total/fumble_recovery_tds fields. No DST labels enter this study. It is a transparent reconstructed offensive score from latest stored source stats, not independently certified DraftKings contest settlement.','', 'Forecasts are retained as originally stored mean/P90 with calibration method/model code-hash lineage; original rows do **not** carry a first-class scoring-definition version or immutable publication evidence for every constituent source. They are the application’s DK offensive forecasts, but cross-version scoring equivalence/source freshness cannot be certified per row. This limits the strength of a “P90 calibration” interpretation. All richer-match paired-difference bootstrap ranges include zero; the basic QB-WR range only reaches zero at its lower edge. These small-cluster ranges are unstable and do not justify a significance claim. Original forecasts were never recomputed with outcomes; no historical cutoff is used as a substitute for actual pregame storage evidence.','', 'Latest eligible forecast selection, slate coverage, changing models, different forecast horizons, salary import availability and prior research inspection create selection bias. Same-game observations share environments, and weeks are not fully independent either. Only one partial season/five weeks is available. Market strata in results.json use the median **stored pregame team implied total**, without a tuned “shootout” cutoff; many cells have few joint hits, so no market-conditioned policy is recommended. Role/share fields remain incomplete and no new numeric allocation probability is invented.','','## Reproduction and next evidence','','[Protocol](PROTOCOL.md) · [Inventory](inventory.json) · [Results including thresholds/strata/weekly counts](results.json) · [Canonical player-game audit](analysis_players.json). Run inventory.py, extract.py, extract_features.py using read-only DB access, then analyze.py and render_report.py; existing JSON inputs are frozen/hashes recorded for exact offline replay. Tests cover scoring/negative points, inclusive thresholds, no unknown-as-zero, identity relations, chronology and clustered summary.','','Prospective logging should append one complete pre-kickoff pool snapshot at fixed horizons, original schedule/role/availability and market source clocks, explicit DK scoring version, model/calibration version and canonical/native IDs. Link corrected final outcomes with source/version separately. Freeze position/workload matching and uncertainty protocol before accumulating more games. Require enough independent weeks and out-of-time full-lineup validation before changing optimizer behavior.']
(P/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');(P/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'protocol_sha256':hashlib.sha256((P/'PROTOCOL.md').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'input_hashes':r['input_hashes'],'analysis_sha256':hashlib.sha256((P/'analyze.py').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'scoring_version':r['scoring_version'],'live_changes':False},indent=2)+'\n')
print('Report saved')
